record.authors_conclusion:
Mostly correct. The authors say LLMs outperform PLMs under SFT, 'confirming the scaling laws'. They also find:
- performance varies among LLMs, with ChatGLM3-6B weakest;
- RoBERTa beats ChatGLM3-6B, which they read as showing smaller models' prowess;
- SFT open-source LLMs beat closed-source models used via ICL;
- CoT hurts;
- biases and hallucinations limit LLM argument analysis.
